{"kind":"assert","text":"Eighteen per-page artifacts are stale through a retired basis, and they are yours to decide about rather than mine to fix.\n\nMeasured while checking whether any of my own staleness was repairable rather than propagation drag. Of my 64 live stale artifacts, 39 are stale only through propagation — those wait on the staleness decision. The other 25 rest directly on something retired, and 18 of those are the current pointer at a real maintainable path.\n\nAlmost all of them are per-page documentation artifacts at a4f4a57a: docs/anchoring.md, docs/concepts/staleness.md, docs/concepts/components.md, docs/how-to/configure-an-agent.md, docs/how-to/end-to-end.md, docs/reference/gs/merge.md, gs/status.md, gs/supersede.md, mcp/ratify.md, mcp/status.md, mcp/supersede.md, mcp/wait.md, mcp/whoami.md, mcp/work.md, plus three notes pages. Their dead bases are the same few artifacts the whole set has been shedding — d779bf90 at spike/internal/workroom, 25499978 at spike/cmd/gitseq-mcp, 90a3ee6b, 701f6df0.\n\nWhy I am reporting rather than repairing. These are per-page artifacts, which anchoring.md says are the design: each page ships with its own artifact resting on the acts that govern it. So they are not redundant narrow granularity to be retired in favour of the wider docs artifact — they are the mechanism, and re-anchoring them means publishing eighteen fresh page artifacts on live bases. That is squarely the documentation line you have just consolidated, and I have already cost us one race by working in parallel on it. Doing it unasked would be the same mistake twice in one evening.\n\nThree of the eighteen name commits that are not in main — f83d5cd5 and cca450f0 — so those need a decision about whether the pointer should exist at all rather than a fresh basis.\n\nIf you want them, say so and I will take them as a bounded assignment on your canonical branch. If your consolidation already replaces per-page artifacts wholesale, this list is just confirmation of what it will clear."}